[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127257,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroma of tendon sheath is a rare benign tumour, presumably of (myo)fibroblastic origin, that arises in the tenosynovial soft tissue, usually attached to a tendon, and occurs predominantly in the upper extremities.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127258,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8813/0 Fibroma of tendon sheath</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127259,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>EE6Y &amp; XH0WB3 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Fibroma of tendon sheath</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127260,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> tenosynovial fibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127261,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127262,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most common sites are the tendons of the fingers, hands, and wrists. Less common sites include the forearm, foot, and knee {27125357; 91424}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127263,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most tumours present as an asymptomatic to mildly painful, small (&lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;mm), slow-growing, and solitary mass, although multiple nodules have also been reported {23212985; 91424; 22028571}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127264,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroma of tendon sheath is rare, with a predilection to occur in middle-aged men {23212985; 27125357; 91424}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127265,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127266,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours have been found to have gene fusions involving <em>USP6</em> and a variety of partners, including <em>PKM</em>, <em>RCC1</em>, <em>ASPN</em>, <em>COL1A1</em>, <em>COL3A1</em>, <em>MYH9</em>, <em>MIR22HG</em>, <em>CTNNB1</em>, <em>SPARC</em>, <em>CAP1</em>, <em>EMP1</em>, <em>CYTOR</em> (<em>LINC00152</em>), <em>NR1D1</em>, <em>RAB1A</em>, and <em>TNC</em> {34088995; 34520696}. They may be a tenosynovial form of nodular fasciitis {32661296}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127267,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroma of tendon sheath is well circumscribed, with a lobulated mass, a uniform grey to white cut surface, and occasional myxoid to cystic change.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127268,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroma of tendon sheath is composed of small to medium-sized bland fibroblastic spindle and stellate cells arranged in fascicles or a storiform pattern, set within a dense fibrocollagenous hyalinized matrix with slit-like spaces and dilated vascular channels. Some myxoid change, extravasated red blood cells, mononuclear inflammatory cells, and (rarely) giant cells can be seen {26729987}. Cellular areas may also be present {91424}. Tumours with unusual histological findings such as a palisading growth pattern, epithelioid cells, and osteoclast-like multinucleated giant cells may have <em>PKM</em> or <em>ASPN</em> as a gene fusion partner {32661296}.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>The differential diagnosis includes nodular fasciitis, myofibroma, and benign fibrous histiocytoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127269,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127270,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>USP6</em> rearrangement may support diagnosis in challenging cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127271,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a well-circumscribed lobulated nodule on tendon; usually hypocellular, with spindle cells in a collagenous background and slit-like vascular spaces.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>USP6</em> rearrangement (in selected or challenging cases).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127272,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127273,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 231,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibroma of tendon sheath is benign but recurs locally in about 25% of cases {91424}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T09:35:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]